# goal The status code is the product

This server usually sits in a failover chain, so the number in the status line is
what the next system acts on. Getting the body right and the status wrong is a
worse failure than returning nothing. The two traps that make a failure look like a
success are in [_.hint#silent_success](../_.hint).

# scope What this module owns

In: routing, authentication, body limits, SSE framing, the timeout and
client-disconnect distinction, and turning errors into OpenAI-shaped bodies.

Out: ACP, agent lifecycle, and translation. It calls `parseChatRequest` and
`Agent.prompt` and does no shape work of its own.

# ui Routes

| method | path | auth | |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/health` | none | liveness plus the configured model ids |
| GET | `/v1/models`, `/models` | yes | OpenAI model list |
| POST | `/v1/chat/completions`, `/chat/completions` | yes | the turn |

`/health` is deliberately unauthenticated: a probe that needs a secret is a probe
that silently stops working when the secret rotates. It exposes model ids and
nothing else.

# invariant Auth compares in constant time, on both header spellings {#auth}

`Authorization: Bearer` and `x-api-key` are both accepted — Anthropic-style clients
send the latter at the same server. Comparison is `timingSafeEqual` with a length
pre-check that returns the same way for every mismatch.

An empty configured `apiKey` disables authentication entirely, and the CLI warns
about it at startup. That is a deployment choice, not an accident to guess at.

# func handleCompletion {#handle}

## flow
1. Read and parse the body under `MAX_BODY_BYTES`.
2. `parseChatRequest` — refusals become 400 here, before any agent is touched.
3. `params.report` — logs and, in `error` mode, rejects.
4. Resolve the model to an agent, or 404 naming what exists.
5. Arm the timeout and the disconnect watcher.
6. Run the turn, streaming or not.
7. Translate the outcome.

## invariant Timeout and disconnect are tracked separately
They need opposite answers: a timeout owes the caller 504, a vanished client owes it
nothing. One flag for both produces a 504 written to a closed socket, or a silent
200 for a request that timed out.

# rule Streaming headers are withheld until the agent produces something {#defer_headers}

`start()` runs on the first streamed event, not before the turn. Committing to
`200 text/event-stream` up front converts every pre-stream failure — including the
429 the chain needs — into a stream that merely stops, which no caller can tell
from a short answer.

Once headers are out the status is spent: mid-stream truncation is reported as
`finish_reason: "length"`, the closest honest value left.

# rule Every response carries an OpenAI-shaped error body {#error_shape}

`{error: {message, type, code, param}}`. Clients branch on `error.code`, so a new
failure mode needs a distinct code, not a new message under an existing one.

# invariant Closing the server closes every agent
Agents are child processes holding authenticated sessions. The `close` handler on
the server is what reaps them, and `bin/acp2api.js` relies on exactly that.

# test server

- `/health` needs no key and lists the models; every other route enforces it
- both header spellings authenticate; a wrong or short key is 401
- an empty `apiKey` accepts everything
- a non-streaming turn returns content, `reasoning_content` and usage
- a streaming turn emits role, deltas and a terminal `finish_reason`, then `[DONE]`
- `stream_options.include_usage` adds a usage-only chunk before `[DONE]`
- a quota failure is 429 **even on a streaming request** — the header-deferral test
- an unrelated failure is 502; an unknown model is 404 naming what is available
- `temperature` returns 200 and reports itself in `x_acp2api.ignored`
- `tools` is 400 and the message points at `mcpServers`
- `unsupportedParams: error` turns the ignorable ones into 400 as well
- `max_tokens` finishes with `length`; `stop` cuts the text and finishes with `stop`
- a timeout is 504, not a truncated 200
- malformed bodies are 400 with an OpenAI-shaped error; unknown routes are 404
- closing the server closes every agent
